steps.do:
Ask, one at a time:
- whether the card is still in their possession;
- whether the PIN may be compromised;
- whether they contacted the merchant (required for non-fraud disputes);
- whether they filed a police report (for fraud over $500; if not, recommend one);
- whether they agree to a written statement;
- when they first noticed it (the discovery date).

Map the customer's PIN answer to a value:
- they shared it → yes_shared;
- they believe it was observed or skimmed → yes_observed;
- not compromised → no;
- unsure → unknown.

Tell the customer three things:
- Rho-Bank submits a chargeback request to the ATM owner/network;
- the investigation can take up to 90 days;
- provisional credit is still required within 10 business days.

Check the four required conditions:
(1) the customer reported within 60 days of the statement date showing the transaction;
(2) the category is unauthorized_transaction, card_present_fraud, card_not_present_fraud, atm_cash_discrepancy or duplicate_charge;
(3) the customer agreed to a written statement;
(4) the account is OPEN with no holds or restrictions.
If all four hold, provisional credit is required: set provisional_credit_eligible to true. Otherwise set it to false. Tell the customer the result.

Confirm each filed dispute to the customer:
- its category;
- whether provisional credit applies: the full amount, reduced by the $50 or $500 liability if reported late, issued within 10 business days (20 for accounts under 30 days old);
- the investigation timeline: 45 business days, or 90 for international transactions, POS outside the US, or new accounts;
- any affidavit due;
- the card action.
Say that provisional credit is reversed only after at least 3 business days' written notice. Name any dispute not filed, and why.
